                    briefing_text_r1:       `You have the strategy pack: channel economics, the Lumo teardown, the IVASS sector letter and the EU AI Act high-risk criteria. Before designing anything, define what transformation means here and map the constraints that bound every option. Lumo took <strong>9% of new motor</strong> in 18 months and your online quote takes <strong>14 minutes</strong> to its 3 — but is the real threat pricing speed, channel economics, data capability, or all three as <strong>one system</strong>? And do you treat the EU AI Act, GDPR, IDD and IVASS as an obstacle to work around, or as a <em>design parameter</em> that shapes the opportunity set itself?`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Choose the digital-transformation path`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Allocate the <strong>EUR 90M</strong> across initiatives and choose the path. <strong>Platform-first</strong> is slow but durable; <strong>channel-first</strong> protects the 78% premium but is slowest against Lumo; <strong>direct-challenger</strong> is fastest share but provokes the agents and carries the highest AI-Act exposure; a <strong>balanced</strong> sequence gates AI behind the platform and the agents. The data platform is the dependency everything sits on — starve it and the AI strands. And set the gating logic: front-load the full €90M and you forfeit the option to learn, <em>and strand capital when a dependency slips</em>.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Intuition vs. analytics: the pay-how-you-drive launch`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Rule on the usage-based motor product. The data model projects a <strong>4-point combined-ratio gain</strong> and share; two veteran underwriters warn of <strong>young-driver mis-pricing</strong> from a model over-fitted to a benign claims period. The EU AI Act requires <em>documented human oversight and bias testing before deployment</em> for exactly this use case. Don't pick one source over the other — the goal is to <strong>combine</strong> them: use the underwriters to interrogate the model's assumptions, and use the data to discipline intuition. A modeled launch with no oversight on a wide book risks an IVASS finding and EUR 12–18M in remediation.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Sequence the change and defend it to the board and regulator`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Sequence the full transformation across 12 quarters and defend it to the board chair and an IVASS supervisor. The order is the strategic core: the <strong>data platform comes before AI underwriting</strong>, and <strong>agent buy-in before any channel shift</strong> — schedule them out of order and the step strands. Show how each high-risk step <em>clears its compliance gate before go-live</em>, build the change plan for the 1,850 agencies so the network is an ally not a casualty, and defend the sequence as gated, not front-loaded.`,

                    r1_threat_label:        `Diagnose the real threat behind the share loss to Lumo.`,
                    r1_box_label:           `How do you treat the regulatory box (EU AI Act, GDPR, IDD, IVASS)?`,
                    r1_thesis_label:        `How sharply do you commit to one transformation thesis the board can hold? (%)`,
